# Build and run artefacts.
#
# Nothing listed here is needed to reproduce a result. `results/*.json` and `figures/` ARE needed --
# every number in the manuscript traces to one of them -- so they are deliberately NOT ignored.

# LaTeX staging directories. build_paper.py writes these; the count reached 48 during development
# because each --build-dir attempt leaves one behind (Windows keeps main.pdf locked if a viewer has
# it open, which is why the override exists at all).
paper_build/

# Compiled output of the staging build. The manuscript PDF that ships lives at paper/main.pdf.
paper_build*/*.pdf

# Page-by-page renders and extracted text used to inspect layout while iterating.
.pagedump/
paper_preview/

# Per-run logs: the console transcripts that produced results/*.json. Kept out of the RELEASE
# (.gitignore) but NOT deleted, because they are the only record of stdout for runs whose JSON has
# been superseded -- and the trace-recovery step in this project read them back once already when a
# parse bug corrupted the per-run files. Deleting evidence that has already been needed once is a
# bad trade for 50 kB. src/check_release.py will keep reporting them under "intermediates"; that
# count is expected to be non-zero and is not a blocker.
logs/
results/*.log

# Python caches.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# matplotlib font cache, created when MPLCONFIGDIR points inside the tree.
.mplconfig/

# Scratch space from repairing the workspace ACL.
.acl-repair/

# Local editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# LaTeX intermediates from build_journal.py. The PDFs next to them are deliverables and ARE
# committed; these are regenerated by the same command that produces them.
paper/journal/*.aux
paper/journal/*.log
paper/journal/*.out

# Local scratch: a copy of a chat answer, not part of the work. It contains this machine's paths.
readme.txt

# Vendor market data. NOT distributed: Alpha Vantage minute bars for nine instruments, and the
# causal preprocessing derived from them. Redistribution is not permitted, so these paths are
# ignored in addition to being absent -- a local copy must not be committable by accident.
# data_manifest/ is deliberately NOT listed: it is metadata (row counts, dates, spread summaries),
# contains no prices, and is shipped.
data/
data_causal/